   "text": {
    "L1": "Three lengths do not always make a triangle. First, find the longest length.",
    "L2": "Check whether the other two lengths add to more than the longest.",
    "L3": "For 6, 8 and 13, the longest is 13, and 6 plus 8 equals 14.",
    "L4": "Because 14 is more than 13, these three lengths can make a triangle.",
    "L5": "If the longest equals the sum of the other two, the shape flattens into a straight line.",
    "L6": "To construct one, draw a side first. Then draw arcs of the other two lengths from its ends.",
    "L7": "The arcs cross at the third vertex. Join that point to both ends of the first side.",
    "L8": "Now use the longest-side check: can 2, 3 and 8 make a triangle?"
   },
